$( <MM> <PROOF_ASST> THEOREM=psiaporthlem1  LOC_AFTER=?

* Lemma for psiaporth: if B is an inverse of A mod Q, the divisibility Q || ( ( B x. N ) - 1 ) says exactly that N lies in the residue class of A.

s1::simp11 |- ( ( ( Q e. NN /\ A e. ZZ /\ B e. ZZ ) /\ Q || ( ( A x. B ) - 1 ) /\ N e. ZZ ) -> Q e. NN )
s2::simp12 |- ( ( ( Q e. NN /\ A e. ZZ /\ B e. ZZ ) /\ Q || ( ( A x. B ) - 1 ) /\ N e. ZZ ) -> A e. ZZ )
